{"name":"Teasel Dipsacus","hex":"#ceaefa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"teasel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants of the genus Dipsacus.","The dried fruiting head of the fuller's teasel, Dipsacus sativa, used for teasing or carding cloth."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To raise the nap on cloth; to tease; to card."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teasel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dipsacus","blocks":[{"text":"Dipsacus is a genus of flowering plant in the family Caprifoliaceae. The members of this genus are known as teasel. The genus includes about 15 species of tall herbaceous biennial plants growing to 1–2.5 metres (3.3–8.2 ft) tall. Dipsacus species are native to Europe, Asia and Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Dipsacus_fullonum1.jpg/330px-Dipsacus_fullonum1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dipsacus","wikidata":"Q161946"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Dipsacus-fullonum-Teasel-seedhead-w-viviparous-germination-PortSunlightRiverPark-UK-23Oct2019.jpg/500px-Dipsacus-fullonum-Teasel-seedhead-w-viviparous-germination-PortSunlightRiverPark-UK-23Oct2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Dipsacus-fullonum-Teasel-seedhead-w-viviparous-germination-PortSunlightRiverPark-UK-23Oct2019.jpg/1280px-Dipsacus-fullonum-Teasel-seedhead-w-viviparous-germination-PortSunlightRiverPark-UK-23Oct2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Dipsacus-fullonum-Teasel-seedhead-w-viviparous-germination-PortSunlightRiverPark-UK-23Oct2019.jpg/500px-Dipsacus-fullonum-Teasel-seedhead-w-viviparous-germination-PortSunlightRiverPark-UK-23Oct2019.jpg?utm_sourc